  "english": "and of Myron [Mersius] the Bishop. [Hymn of] Martyrs:\nIn the melody: \"They Were Amazed\" (Hiatsan). Midday Hymn,\nTone 2 [b3 - Bz]: \"Who with Light\" (Or lusov).\n\n26. Sunday, Tone 3 [AGDz - AGdz], First. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 8 [ak - Ak]: \"Unoriginate Word\" (Anskizbn band). Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [adz - Adz]: \"With the Women\" (End kanaysn), and \"Who Ineffable\" (Or anchar).\n\n27. Monday, Tone 2 [AK - Ak], Julian and Basil,\nand Indus, and the others. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts],\nTone 2 [b3 - Bz]: \"Without Malice\" (Anokhakal).\n\nDECEMBER\n\n3. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK - Dk], Second. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 4 [b] - Bk]: \"Incorruptible\" (Anapakan). Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 8 [dk - Dk]: \"The Angel [of the Lord]\" (Hreshtak).\n\n4. Monday, Tone 1 [ADz - Adz], Gennarius and Mercurius,\nand James and Jovasap [Iravap'ar].\n\n5. Tuesday, Tone 2 [AK - Ak], King Abgar.\nReadings and Gospel as on the feast of Theodosius.\n\n[Unreadable text / Typographical artifacts]\n\n9. Saturday, Tone 8 [DK - Dk], Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n\n10. Sunday, Tone 7 [DZ - Dz], Third. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 4 [bk - Bk]: \"Unoriginate God\" (Anskizbn astuats). Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 7 [dz - Dz]: \"Who art Above\" (Or i verat es). Eve of the Fast of Saint James [Surb Hakob].\n\n13. Wednesday, Tone 2 [AK - Ak], Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] of Fasting, Tone 7 [dz - Dz]: \"Who [delivered] the Three Children\" (Or zeris mankunsn).\n\n17. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK - Gk], Fourth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 5 [g3 - Gz]: \"Glorified Son\" (Paravoryal vordi). Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 6 [gk - Gk]: \"Having Taken and Ours\" (Aryal yev mer).\n\n23. Saturday, Tone 4 [BK - Bk], David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n24. Sunday, Tone 5 [GZ - Gz], Fifth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 6 [gk - Gk]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhahavitean). Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [g3 - Gz]: \"Oil-bearing and Holy\" (Yughaber yev surb), to the end.\n\n29. Friday, Tone 2 [AK - Ak], Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n\n30. Saturday, Tone 3 [BZ - Bz], Fast of the Nativity of Christ; and of the Patriarchs Basil and the others.\n\n31. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK - Bk], Sixth [Sunday of Advent], Fasting. Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 4 [bk - Bk]: \"The Women Anticipated\" (Kankhetsin kanayqn), to the end.\nAnd the rest see according to the order.\n\nJANUARY\n\n1. Monday, Tone 5 [GZ - Gz], Fasting. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 8 [dk - Dk]: \"Blessed art thou, Lord, God of our Fathers\" (Hartsn merots orhneal es ter).\n\n5. Friday, Tone 1 [ADz - Adz], Eve of the Nativity of Christ our God.\n\n[Unreadable text / Typographical artifacts]\n\nROMAN EPACT: 6.\n\nJANUARY\n\n6. THURSDAY, Tone 5 [GZ - Gz], Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The meat-eating period [between feasts] is thirty-two days.\n\n15. Saturday, Tone 6 [GK - Gk], John the Forerunner.\n\n16. Sunday, Tone 7 [DZ - Dz], First. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 8 [dk - Dk]: \"Dawning\" (Tsagumn). Lord's Prayer / Evening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 5 [g3 - Gz]: \"Awesome\" (Ahagin).\n\n17. Monday, Tone 8 [DK - Dk], Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n\n18. Tuesday, Tone 1 [ADz - Adz], Anthony, and Triphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the Hermits.\n\n19. Wednesday, Tone 2 [AK - Ak], Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] of Fasting, Tone 2 [b] - Bz]: \"Who didst Save\" (Or apretsuts'er).\n\n20. Thursday, Tone 3 [BZ - Bz], King Theodosius and the Holy Children of Ephesus.\n\n22. Saturday, Tone 5 [GZ - Gz], Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n\n23. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK - Gk], Second. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts], Tone 5 [g3 - Gz]: \"Who...\"",
